<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20944] LNet: errors detected while forwarding a message escape the health check</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20944</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Problem&lt;br/&gt;
A router that marked a peer NI down drops every message routed to that&lt;br/&gt;
peer but never degrades its health. The peer NI stays at&lt;br/&gt;
LNET_MAX_HEALTH_VALUE, so it is never queued for recovery, no recovery&lt;br/&gt;
ping is sent, and the router black-holes the peer until LNet restarts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen in LUS-13527: 5 of 13 routers black-holed an MDS peer for ~30&lt;br/&gt;
minutes, evicting clients. Fingerprint on an affected router:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;state: down&lt;br/&gt;
health value: 1000&lt;br/&gt;
Root cause&lt;br/&gt;
On a router the forward runs inside lnet_finalize(): it health checks&lt;br/&gt;
the receive leg, then lnet_complete_msg_locked() calls lnet_send() to&lt;br/&gt;
forward (lib-msg.c:411-433). The forward fails in&lt;br/&gt;
lnet_post_send_locked(), which skips lnet_finalize() because do_send is&lt;br/&gt;
false, and the error returns to "if (rc != 0) goto again;" and is&lt;br/&gt;
discarded. The health check already ran, for the receive.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two effects hide it: msg_ev.status is still 0 while msg_health_status is&lt;br/&gt;
not, which lnet_is_health_check() rejects as inconsistent; and&lt;br/&gt;
lnet_send() overwrites the precise status with REMOTE_ERROR.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same gap applies to the ACK send, not just routed forwards.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
